    "result_text": "The full test suite passes (BUILD SUCCESS). \n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the rule that rejects creating an owner when the owner's city already contains 50 or more owners, responding with **409 Conflict**.\n\nChanges, all following the existing conventions for the other owner-creation conflict rules (duplicate telephone/household):\n\n1. **`OwnerCityAtCapacityException`** (new) \u2014 a `RuntimeException` carrying the offending city, mirroring `DuplicateOwnerTelephoneException`.\n\n2. **`OwnerRestControllerV1`** \u2014 added a `rejectCityAtCapacity(city)` check in `addOwner(...)`, plus a `MAX_OWNERS_PER_CITY = 50` constant. It counts existing owners whose city matches case-insensitively (the same matching used by `nextCustomerCode`) and throws when the count is \u2265 50.\n\n3. **`ExceptionControllerAdvice`** \u2014 added an `@ExceptionHandler` for the new exception that renders it as a 409 via the existing `conflict(...)` helper, with an `errors: [\"city\"]` array, consistent with the other conflict responses.\n\nThe provided acceptance test (`coreRejectsWhenCityAtCapacity` \u2014 fills a city to 50, expects the 51st to get 409) passes, and the full suite is green.",
